    "youtube_title": "Why rose gold is pink",
    "caption": "Rose gold is pink because of copper. 18 karat gold is 75% gold, and the other metals set the color. Yellow gold adds mostly silver and a little copper, rose gold mostly copper, and white gold adds palladium or nickel and then gets a rhodium coat that jewelers redo about once a year. Every ring in this video is a render made from a 3D file with HeyGema.",
